**Schedule amendment.** Under §2.3’s mapping, `build ms = segment-relative ms − 1000`. F-5500 maps to build **4500 ms**, when the dice are already in the hands. CP6 maps to **5000 ms**, when the scoop continues. §2.1 starts gathering at **5000 ms**, and §2.3 explicitly requires `gatherP = 0` there. That leaves the planned slab stationary at F-5500 and puts the start of motion at CP6. Move gather onset earlier, add a named cube-departure predicate for **4500 ms** and an in-progress predicate for **5000 ms**, and preserve bowl completion at **6000 ms**. Add the omitted F-2500 and F-3500 rows at build **1500 ms** and **2500 ms**. The hand omission can carry the former as a settled-cushion analogue, and P3 already supplies the mid-press state for the latter. The count arithmetic is consistent with the supplied census description: 3 columns × 3 rows × 2 layers = **18 cubes**.

**Reductions.** §2.2 names the prior-episode tail, hands, separate bowl shot, and spare pincushions. Also record the staggered reveal as a deliberate replacement for the abrupt CP4→F-4500 source reveal. §2.5 identifies the change, and §2.2 is where it belongs as a fidelity departure.

**Limits.** This verdict uses the supplied §1–§2 record, guard excerpt, and gate-return summaries. The standalone wave manifest, governing instruction and amendment files, family score files, and source frames were unavailable for independent assessment. The supplied guard excerpt lists commands 1–7, so §2.3’s reference to command 8 is **UNVERIFIED**.

